    "summary": "Burmese kalaga, made of red wool and decorated in applique with braid, sequins, paper, felt and cotton. In the centre is a sequence of three narrative panels separated by flowering trees, The narrative is unknown but the first is a palace scene, the second takes place in the forest and the third is located by a small tank. The heroine wears a distinctive deer-headdress. There is a decorative border around the edge. It is backed with red cloth.",
